{
  "name": "Interrupted and Restricted",
  "parent_id": 203314133681389,
  "group_id": "6e2b257e-e43b-410e-8840-acc17921f72c",
  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-31T09:23:51.614Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-07-31T09:23:51.703Z",
  "published_at": "2026-07-31T09:23:51.689Z",
  "id": 203981748721001,
  "uuid": "5599e458-94c5-43a4-9215-ad102f44608b",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "513b98c4-7395-75b4-ca50-4647be8a620e",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "2356263c-e874-7e77-2523-683e1dd17daf",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "This panel seeks to address not only the forward facing aspects of digital humanities (DH), ensuring access to researchers, students, and scholars, but also taking a step back to question the ethics and implications of what is disseminated via the virtual vis-à-vis human rights.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "As chair and moderator, Sharon Smith will lead this international panel-consisting of three distinct presentations (one presentation will have two presenters), including a journalist, cultural heritage (NGOs), academics, and librarians-in examining practitioners' ethical responsibilities beyond the realm of preservation and sustainability, both critical to DH writ large. The panel will focus on DH in MENASA regions and examine:",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "1. The politics of digitisation in light of digital divide, accessibility, and digital colonialism.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "2. The successes and failures of DH praxes within cultural heritage organisations with regard to identification (objects and sites), looting, commodification, and illegal exchange of materials.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "3. As stewards of materials in their possession, what ethical obligation they have to \"do no harm\" and what that means for a politically charged collection, the release of which could be seen as contributing to a humanitarian crisis.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Register now and join us online via Zoom",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "https://aku-edu.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJ0qduispjkjGNYwvUw1p97r9pWi4hr-Gvc-",
                        "uuid": null,
                        "anchor": null,
                        "custom": {},
                        "target": "_blank",
                        "linktype": "url"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": ".",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Moderator",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Sharon Smith is an Associate Academic serving as Curator for the Middle East, North Africa, Global South, History, and Religion at ASU Library. Smith is engaged in projects at ASU with the Institute for Humanities Research, the Center for Religion and Conflict, and the School of Historical, Philosophical, and Religious Studies. She has served on numerous committees and boards including as a Participating Expert for UNESCO's Safeguarding of Syria's Cultural Heritage Committee. Currently, she is a Fellow at the Tangier American Legation in Morocco (TALIM).",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Discussant",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Walid Ghali",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "is the Head of the Aga Khan Library, London, Assistant Professor at the Aga Khan University's Institute for the Study of Muslim Civilisations and a Chartered Librarian of the Chartered Institute of Library and Information Professionals (CILIP). Also, he is a member of the Islamic Manuscript Association, University of Cambridge. Dr Ghali received his PhD from Cairo University, Faculty of Arts in 2012. His current research projects focus on the Islamic manuscript traditions, particularly in Arabic script, and the history of books.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Speakers",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "John Carlson is an Associate Professor of Religious Studies at Arizona State University where he directs the Center for the Study of Religion and Conflict and co-directs the Recovering Truth project. He is currently working on two books: a monograph on justice and an edited collection on religion and global citizenship.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Anand Gopal is an award-winning journalist and Assistant Research Professor with the Center for the Study of Religion and Conflict and the Center on the Future of War at Arizona State University. He holds a PhD in sociology from Columbia University, and specialises in ethnographically based data journalism. Gopal has reported extensively on Afghanistan, Syria, and Iraq, writing for",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": " Harpers, The New Yorker, The Wall Street Journal, The Christian Science Monitor",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "italic"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": ", and other publications, while also producing scholarship based on his fieldwork and complex network analysis.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Peter Herdrich is the Co-founder of the Antiquities Coalition, the pre-eminent international NGO in the fight against the looting and illicit trade in cultural heritage property. He currently oversees publishing at the Antiquities Coalition Think Tank and directs digital cultural heritage projects with the Ministry of Culture and Arts in Algeria and regionally in the Maghreb. He is the Chief Executive Officer of the Cultural Capital Group, consulting with clients across the cultural heritage, communications, and library sectors.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Organiser",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                },
                {
                  "text": "This event is organised by the Aga Khan Library, London.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Registration",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Register for the panel discussion and join us online via Zoom by clicking ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "here",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "https://aku-edu.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJ0qduispjkjGNYwvUw1p97r9pWi4hr-Gvc-",
                        "uuid": null,
                        "anchor": null,
                        "custom": {},
                        "target": "_blank",
                        "linktype": "url"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": ".",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
